  "title": "Sammuramat",
  "summary": "Sammuramat was wife of the Assyrian king Shamshi-Adad V (reigned 824–811 BCE) and, after his death, regent for their young son Adad-nirari III for three, possibly five, years. A stele naming her, dated c. 809 BCE, comes from Ashur and is in the Pergamon Museum, Berlin. Little else is known of her.",
